  "generated_text": "To determine the residue of \\(-811 \\pmod{24}\\), we need to find an integer \\(r\\) such that \\(-811 \\equiv r \\pmod{24}\\) and \\(0 \\leq r < 24\\).\n\nFirst, we perform the division of \\(-811\\) by \\(24\\):\n\n\\[\n-811 \\div 24 \\approx -33.791667\n\\]\n\nThe integer part of the quotient is \\(-34\\). Now, we calculate the remainder by multiplying \\(-34\\) by \\(24\\) and subtracting the result from \\(-811\\):\n\n\\[\n-34 \\times 24 = -816\n\\]\n\n\\[\n-811 - (-816) = -811 + 816 = 5\n\\]\n\nThus, the remainder when \\(-811\\) is divided by \\(24\\) is \\(5\\). \n\nTherefore, the residue of \\(-811 \\pmod{24}\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{5}\n\\]",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[5, '5']",
    "gold_answer": "Dividing 811 by 24 gives a quotient of 33, so the greatest multiple of 24 less than $-811$ is $24\\cdot -34=-816$. Thus $-811$ is $-811-(-816)=5$ more than a multiple of $24$. Since $0\\leq 5 < 24$, the residue of $-811$ is $\\boxed{5}$ (mod 24).",
    "is_correct": true
  },
